WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.191
Week 33: History, Society, and Multiple Perspectives. summarize a historical development distinguish fact from interpretation compare perspectives

2
00:00:10.191 --> 00:00:18.015
Form and meaning. Past perfect; reported evidence; concessive clauses; cause, consequence, and counterargument.

3
00:00:18.015 --> 00:00:55.345
Model set. La fuente afirma que la reforma amplió derechos. Otros sostienen que la desigualdad continuó. Cuando cambió el gobierno, muchas personas ya habían emigrado. Aunque existe consenso sobre los hechos, su significado se debate. El testimonio aporta una perspectiva personal. The source states that the reform expanded rights. Others maintain that inequality continued. When the government changed, many people had already emigrated. Although there is consensus about the facts, their meaning is debated. The testimony provides a personal perspective.

4
00:00:55.345 --> 00:01:05.475
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:01:05.475 --> 00:01:19.338
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: summarize a historical development; distinguish fact from interpretation; compare perspectives. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:19.338 --> 00:01:57.649
Model language. La fuente afirma que la reforma amplió derechos. — The source states that the reform expanded rights. Otros sostienen que la desigualdad continuó. — Others maintain that inequality continued. Cuando cambió el gobierno, muchas personas ya habían emigrado. — When the government changed, many people had already emigrated. Aunque existe consenso sobre los hechos, su significado se debate. — Although there is consensus about the facts, their meaning is debated. El testimonio aporta una perspectiva personal. — The testimony provides a personal perspective.

7
00:01:57.649 --> 00:02:07.803
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
